# go.boilerplate — Project Purpose

Production-ready Go HTTP API starter: auth, email, Docker, OpenAPI, AI quality gates.

Add product features as new `src/modules/<name>` packages — do not grow chat/friends domains here.

**Design doc (source of truth):** `docs/DESIGN_DOC.md`  
**Agent guide:** `AGENTS.md`

## Architecture

- `src/middleware/` — shared Fiber + Huma auth middleware
- `src/openapi/` — Huma OpenAPI config, `/docs` playground, `/openapi.json`
- `src/modules/<name>/router.go` — Huma operations only
- `src/modules/<name>/handlers/` — thin HTTP handlers
- `src/modules/<name>/services/` — business logic
- `src/modules/<name>/repositories/` — GORM (use Preload/Joins)
- `src/routes/routes.go` — wire modules

## Before finishing any task

```bash
make ai-check
make test
make build
```

Update `docs/DESIGN_DOC.md` when changing API, models, routes, or Docker.

## Project skills

- **create-db-entity** — `.cursor/skills/create-db-entity/SKILL.md`
- **create-email-template** — `.cursor/skills/create-email-template/SKILL.md` (Go Boilerplate emails from Figma Protocol)

## Do not

- Put GORM/DB logic in handlers or routers
- Skip tests for new code
- Commit secrets
- Mix 3+ contexts in one file (HTTP + DB + routing)
- Query inside loops without Preload/batch
